  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1252 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nSaturday through Thursday:\n\nTemperatures will quickly recover on Saturday as the low exits\nand strong high pressure sets up over the Midwest. Yet another\nsurface trough developing in the Northern Plains will keep our\npressure gradient tight over WI on Sat, so expect breezy\nsouthwest winds (but only to around 25 mph) and highs \nrecovering into the mid to upper 50s. Breezy southwest winds \nwill continue Sunday and highs should manage to reach the lower\n60s.\n\nThe warm-up will continue through Thursday as we largely remain\nin southerly flow. Highs will be in the 60s, but get up to \naround 70 by Wednesday. \n\nThe weather will remain largely dry from Saturday through\nThursday. There is one weak shortwave that cold bring a period\nof clouds and a few sprinkles Wed nt. \n\nCronce",
